\f0\fs24 \cf0 Documentation:\
Nuclear war impacts on fish catches by country.\
Original data from Scherrer et al., 2020, PNAS, \'93Marine wild-capture fisheries after nuclear war\'94.\
\
These files contain model output from the BOATS model for fish catches by exclusive economic zone (EEZ) under six different nuclear war scenarios. Each nuclear war scenario is presented in a separate file (5Tg, 16Tg, 27Tg, 37Tg, 47Tg, and 150Tg). Model output comes from a business-as-usual fishing scenario, assuming that there is no change in fishing dynamics (see Scherrer et al). \
\
Variables:\
EEZ: name of the exclusive economic zone\
EEZ_no: index of the exclusive economic zone\
EEZ_area: area of the exclusive economic zone (km2)\
catch_diff_mean_yrX: mean absolute change in EEZ catch relative to control simulation for year X after the war (gram wet biomass) \
\pard\tx566\tx1133\tx1700\tx2267\tx2834\tx3401\tx3968\tx4535\tx5102\tx5669\tx6236\tx6803\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 catch_diff_mean_yrX: standard deviation of the absolute reduction in EEZ catch (gram wet biomass)\
catch_diff_perc_mean_yrX: mean percent change in EEZ catch relative to control simulation (gram wet biomass) for year X after the war (%)\
catch_diff_perc_std_yrX: standard deviation of the percent change in EEZ catch (%)\
catch_ctrl_mean_yr1: mean total EEZ catch in the control simulation (no war) for year X post-war (gram wet biomass)\
catch_ctrl_std_yr1: standard deviation of total EEZ catch in the control simulation (no war) for year X post-war (gram wet biomass)\
catch_NW_scenario_mean_yrX: mean total EEZ catch in the nuclear war simulation for year X post-war (gram wet biomass)\
catch_NW_scenario_std_yrX: standard deviation of total EEZ catch in the nuclear war simulation for year X post-war (gram wet biomass)\
